@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the credential work that is NOT built — brokering for mixin kits, then retiring env-carried keys behind the init surface that already ships
' OPEN WORK ONLY. Everything an operator can already do today was moved out on
' 2026-09-16; if a section here describes shipped behaviour, it is in the wrong
' file. No `covers:` lines: _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule,
' and a plan claiming shipped files fires the drift guard twice for one change.
'   what SHIPPED, and where it is drawn:
'     _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-wireframe.puml  the list, its fields, and
'                                                      the store-naming scheme
'     _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-entry.puml      the field rules + verify
'   the decision this implements ... _spec/_plans/host-held-provider-keys.puml
'   where a secret rests ........... _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml
'   the file P3 retires ............ _spec/_plans/workspace-env-key.puml
'   who injects on sbx today ....... _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'   what the agent may hold ........ _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'   the gate that decides a service  _spec/internal/sbx/kit-sandbox-credential-gap.puml
'   the code the open work touches:
'     internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go:667,689 (agentCredentials, Spec) — the
'       ownAgent gate — real, still there, and NOT what produced the 401
'     internal/run/run.go (resolveCredentials, StoreHeld) — where P2's precedence
'       would go, and where nothing decides one today
'     internal/sbx/secret.go (SecretSetArgs), internal/sbx/run.go (StoredSecretNames)
'
' ── THE PENDING ACTION, IN THREE STEPS ─────────────────────────────────────
' Read this much and you can start. Everything after it is evidence for why.
'
'   1 DECLARE   STRUCK 2026-09-16 — MOOT, and it was the largest item here.
'               It read: lift `agentCredentials` out of the `if ownAgent` branch
'               and set `kit.Credentials` on the MIXIN kit too. Measured since:
'               TestOpenCodeAuth/zen/broker PASSES at 200 where it returned 401,
'               and TestClaudeCodeAuth/api-key/broker reaches the provider. sbx's
'               proxy injects for its BUILT-IN services on a mixin kit as soon as
'               the store entry carries the SERVICE name, so proveo never needed
'               to declare `kit.Credentials`. The `ownAgent` gate is real, still
'               there, and was never what produced the 401 — the store entry's
'               name was. See _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml.
'   2 RESOLVE   DONE by the same change: `credentials.StoreName` looks the id up
'               through the provider registry rather than trimming `_API_KEY`,
'               and keeps api keys and plan tokens on separate ids.
'   3 UNSKIP    STILL OPEN, and now the only one. `TestSandboxKitProxyManagesThe-
'               Credential` is gated behind PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1, so the gap
'               reported green throughout — including while the bug was real and
'               while it was being fixed. Nothing pins the behaviour in a normal
'               suite until this runs there.
'
' Then the three retirement steps below (P2, P3, P4) become safe to take.
'
' ── THE TWO MECHANISMS, BECAUSE THE WHOLE SUBJECT IS THE DIFFERENCE ────────
' `--credentials` picks WHO HOLDS THE KEY while the agent runs:
'
'   broker    the value stays in sbx's host-wide secret store under the SERVICE
'             id its proxy authenticates by. The agent is given nothing; sbx's
'             proxy substitutes the real header on the way out. WORKS on sbx as
'             of 72848db, and is the only posture that backend offers.
'   forward   proveo puts the value in the agent's own environment. That is the
'             posture sbx no longer offers — the credential would sit inside the
'             sandbox with the model. It remains real on the docker rendering,
'             and remains the only route for a credential the proxy cannot
'             attach (B4, _spec/_plans/host-held-provider-keys.puml).
'
' WHERE sbx IS IN THIS. proveo does not run the sandbox or the proxy; it renders
' a Kit and hands it over. The proxy attaches headers for sbx's own BUILT-IN
' services, and it does that on a mixin Kit without proveo declaring anything —
' which is the fact the superseded section below gets wrong. What proveo owns is
' narrow and was the whole defect: writing the store entry under a name the proxy
' looks for.
'
' ── THE EVIDENCE — SUPERSEDED 2026-09-16, KEPT VERBATIM ───────────────────
' Everything from here to the end of this section was the diagnosis before the
' measurement, and it is WRONG about the cause. It is kept word for word because
' it is the intuitive reading: a missing `credentials:` block in a YAML file is
' visible, and a store entry under the wrong name is not, so the next person to
' look will reach for this explanation again.
'
' What is true: the `ownAgent` gate exists and a mixin kit carries no
' `credentials:` block. What is false: that this is why broker returned 401.
' sbx's proxy injects for its BUILT-IN services without proveo declaring
' anything — measured, TestOpenCodeAuth/zen/broker now passes at 200. The cause
' was the store entry's NAME. See _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml.
'
' Why `ownAgent` is false for every def but cecli:
' `ownAgent := !in.Shell && sbx.DeclaresOwnAgent(harness)`, which is
' `BuiltinAgent(target) == "" && AgentKitEnabled()` — and claudecode→claude,
' opencode→opencode, cursor→cursor, codex→codex all map to a built-in sbx
' agent, so proveo renders a mixin and the credentials branch never runs.
'
' A SECOND DEFECT, SMALLER AND SEPARABLE: the run header prints "broker: N
' providers injected at the egress layer (…)" whatever the backend. True of the
' docker rendering, where a sidecar does inject. False under sbx. That line is a
' claim about something that did not happen and can be fixed on its own.
'
' Measured 2026-09-15, one run, one key:
'
'   OPENCODE_API_KEY  --credentials forward  POST /zen/v1/chat/completions  200
'   OPENCODE_API_KEY  --credentials broker   same endpoint, same key        401
'   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY --credentials broker   same shape, other provider     401
'
' The credential is good — forward spends it. The rendered kit says why:
' `proveo run opencode --credentials broker --print` writes
' <state>/egress/<sid>/sbx/kit/spec.yaml, and that file is 41 lines of
' `kind: mixin` with permissions, environment and setup — and NO `credentials:`
' block. Nothing is broken in the proxy: it was never asked to manage a
' credential.
'
' NAMING IS NECESSARY AND INSUFFICIENT, and this was tested rather than assumed.
' `sbx secret set --force opencode` was given the SAME key that forward spends
' successfully; `sbx secret ls` then showed `opencode (stored)`, so an arbitrary
' name IS storable — sbx's "available services" list is the set it has built-in
' knowledge for, not a whitelist. TestOpenCodeAuth/zen re-run:
'
'   forward  200      broker  401      unchanged
'
' So a correctly-named store entry does not produce a working broker path —
' which is why step 1 comes before step 2, not instead of it.
'
' ── WHY THE KINDS MUST BE DISTINGUISHABLE ──────────────────────────────────
' The one result nobody recovers by reading the code, because the code does not
' do it yet. Measured the day the naming scheme was decided: a subscription was
' stored as `anthropic` to test the naming hypothesis, and
' TestClaudeCodeAuth/api-key/broker still returned 401 — CORRECTLY, because the
' probe authenticates as an API KEY and the proxy was attaching an OAuth token
' into an `x-api-key` header.
'
' One id per provider cannot carry both kinds, and a store that hides the
' difference turns a naming fix into a silent 401. init already keeps them apart
' on the write side (`subscriptionStore`); the broker side has to keep them apart
' on the read side, and must resolve ids through the registry rather than
' re-deriving them from env var names — the six canonical exceptions are listed
' with the scheme in _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-wireframe.puml.
'
' ── RETIRING ENV-CARRIED CREDENTIALS: P2, P3, P4 ───────────────────────────
' P1 ADDITIVE is done — init writes the store, env keeps working unchanged, and
' an untouched amber field imports on accept. The three below are open.
'
' THE ORDER CANNOT CHANGE, and that is the whole reason this is staged: removing
' the env path before the store can be filled leaves an operator with no way in.
' Each step also has to be observable before the next one is safe, because each
' one takes away a surface somebody is relying on.
'
'   P2 PREFERRED  RESHAPED 2026-09-16, and it is no longer only about reading.
'                 proveo RE-STORES from the env on every run, so a stale env
'                 value silently OVERWRITES a good store entry — the precedence
'                 question now has a write side that decides it before any reader
'                 gets a say. A store entry must outrank the env var of the same
'                 provider in both directions: not overwritten by it, and
'                 preferred over it at resolve time. The run header must say
'                 which won and why — sbx-secret-store-is-global is the hazard
'                 this must not repeat. Nothing decides it today: `StoreHeld`
'                 (run.go:358) sets `LoggedIn` and a report line, and no reader
'                 ranks them.
'   P3 WARNED     a run that finds a key only in the workspace .env warns with
'                 the move command; workspace-env-key.puml is the file that
'                 retires here. Cannot precede P2 — warning an operator off a
'                 surface that still wins is telling them to break their setup.
'   P4 REFUSED    NOW A DOCKER-ONLY STEP. forward stops accepting a plaintext key
'                 for any provider the proxy can inject. On sbx that already
'                 happened: the credentials row still draws forward and gates it,
'                 and the backend ignores a manifest that still names forward, so
'                 P4 has nothing left to refuse there. What remains is the docker
'                 rendering, where forward is still a real posture.
'                 B4 keeps its exception either way: providers that CANNOT be
'                 injected — AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS
'                 and four more — keep a host-resolvable reference and still
'                 forward, which is the one hole credential-boundary.puml's
'                 property has left (_spec/_plans/host-held-provider-keys.puml).
'
' Nothing here changes credential-boundary.puml's property. The agent holds
' sentinels either way; this changes only where the real value rests between
' runs and who put it there.
'
' ── WHAT CLOSING THIS DOES AND DOES NOT FIX ────────────────────────────────
' Countable rather than hopeful, against the 2026-09-15 suite's eleven failures:
'   ALREADY FIXED        the three broker 401s, by 72848db naming the store
'                        entry for the SERVICE. "Necessary and insufficient" was
'                        the wrong conclusion: the experiment behind it stored a
'                        correct name by hand while proveo went on writing the
'                        env-var-named entry beside it, so the run still resolved
'                        proveo's. Naming was sufficient.
'   ALREADY ADDRESSED    the chrome-bridge early exit, whose cause is a login
'                        the provider refuses. `verifySlot` ships, so init
'                        reports the refusal rather than calling it done.
'   NOT CREDENTIALS      the other seven — --local-model never reaching the
'                        agent, subprojects carrying no _spec or git under sbx,
'                        the kit shape, the settings cache. None of this touches
'                        them and it must not be offered as though it does.
'
' The suite rule that follows: a test whose credential is ABSENT or UNSPENDABLE
' skips, naming the provider and the init command that provisions it. A test
' whose credential is PROVABLY GOOD — forward returns 200 — may never skip on a
' 401. That is the defect, and skipping it is how the defect stops being
' reported.

title OPEN — brokering works on sbx and nothing pins it in a normal suite;\nthen the env path retires in three steps

component "**the only open step**\nunskip TestSandboxKitProxyManagesTheCredential" as UNSKIP <<error>>

node "the host" as HOST <<host>> {
  database "sbx secret store\nentry named for the SERVICE\n— fixed in 72848db" as STORE <<db>>
}

node "sbx" as SBX <<host>> {
  component "sbx proxy\nattaches for its BUILT-IN services,\non a mixin Kit, undeclared" as PROXY <<cloud>>
  node "the sandbox (VM)" as VM <<host>> {
    component "the agent\nholds nothing spendable" as AGENT <<app>>
  }
}

cloud "the provider\nbroker: 200" as PROV <<cloud>>

STORE ARROW_MAIN PROXY : read by service id
AGENT ARROW_MAIN PROXY : request, no credential
PROXY ARROW_MAIN PROV : real header attached outbound
UNSKIP ARROW_ERROR PROXY : nothing pins this in a normal suite

note bottom of STORE
  **The name was the whole defect.** proveo wrote
  the entry under the ENV VAR; the proxy looks up
  the SERVICE. One good key, one unread entry, and
  a 401 that read as a broker bug.
end note

note right of PROXY
  **It never needed proveo to declare it.**
  Measured: broker reaches the provider on a mixin
  Kit with no ""credentials:"" block. The ownAgent
  gate is real and was never the cause.
end note

note bottom of UNSKIP
  **A gap that reported green.**
  ""PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1"" gated the one test that
  covers this, so the suite stayed quiet while the
  bug was live and while it was fixed.
end note

package "then the env path retires" as RETIRE {
  component "P2 store outranks env\nBOTH ways: not overwritten,\nand preferred at resolve" as P2 <<app>>
  component "P3 .env-only key\nnames the move command" as P3 <<app>>
  component "P4 docker only\nsbx already refuses forward" as P4 <<app>>
}

P2 ARROW_MAIN P3 : only after
P3 ARROW_MAIN P4 : only after
KIT ARROW_OPTIONAL P4 : P4 waits on the Kit being fixed

note bottom of P4
  **The order is the design.** Take the env path
  away before the store is preferred, or before
  brokering works, and an operator is left with
  no route that authenticates.
end note

@enduml
